From: GloriousEggroll <gloriouseggroll@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] dxgi: Allow keeping fullscreen presentation on focus loss.

FFXIV shrinks from emulated fullscreen to its saved 1280x720 window when
focus moves to another monitor. Captures from both XWayland and Wine-Wayland
show the same sequence: foreground loss, a roughly 100 ms delay, then the
desktop-mode restore and decorated-window restore. Wine-Wayland keeps the
3840x2160 fullscreen surface until that restore; it does not initially
shrink the surface on keyboard leave.

This matches DXGI's foreground-loss occlusion handling, which calls
SetFullscreenState(FALSE) from Present or GetFullscreenState. With Wine's
fullscreen emulation that tears down scaling even though the game could
remain fullscreen in the background.

Add dxgi.keepFullscreenOnFocusLoss, disabled by default, and enable it for
ffxiv_dx11.exe. Suppress both the implicit fullscreen exit and the
focus-only DXGI_STATUS_OCCLUDED result, including DXGI_PRESENT_TEST, so an
application polling presentation does not get an inconsistent state.
Keep the existing minimized-window handling and do not change explicit
SetFullscreenState calls, input focus, or D3D9. Continue to defer D3D12
fullscreen resolution updates while unfocused.

This is a scoped compatibility behavior, not a global change to DXGI's
fullscreen semantics. Other games can opt in through DXVK_CONFIG for
comparison without changing Wine or either overlay bridge. Black Desert
has not yet been validated with this option.

Issue: https://github.com/GloriousEggroll/proton-ge-custom/issues/639

Runtime validation pending:
- FFXIV: fullscreen 1920x1080 on a 3840x2160 desktop; click another monitor
  and Alt+Tab out/back. Confirm full-size presentation without game input.
- Switch to windowed mode explicitly; verify the saved window is restored.
- Minimize/restore, change fullscreen resolution, and exit normally.
- Repeat with XWayland and Wine-Wayland, with and without the overlay.
- Set dxgi.keepFullscreenOnFocusLoss = False to compare the old behavior.
- Check an unrelated game retains its existing fullscreen-loss behavior.

---
diff --git a/dxvk.conf b/dxvk.conf
index 33002dd..254d3fc 100644
--- a/dxvk.conf
+++ b/dxvk.conf
@@ -73,6 +73,18 @@
 # dxgi.deferInitialFullscreen = False
 
 
+# Keep a non-minimized DXGI fullscreen swapchain when keyboard focus moves
+# to another window. Prevents the automatic desktop-mode and window-size
+# restore from dropping Wine's fullscreen upscaling. Focus and input still
+# belong to the newly activated window.
+# Explicit fullscreen/windowed requests and minimized-window handling remain
+# unchanged. This does not affect D3D9 and is enabled by default for FFXIV.
+#
+# Supported values: True, False
+
+# dxgi.keepFullscreenOnFocusLoss = False
+
+
 # Enforce a stricter maximum frame latency. Overrides the application
 # setting specified by calling IDXGIDevice::SetMaximumFrameLatency.
 # Setting this to 0 will have no effect.
diff --git a/src/dxgi/dxgi_options.cpp b/src/dxgi/dxgi_options.cpp
index b5bae6a..d539111 100644
--- a/src/dxgi/dxgi_options.cpp
+++ b/src/dxgi/dxgi_options.cpp
@@ -177,6 +177,7 @@ namespace dxvk {
     // We don't support dcomp swapchains and some games may rely on them failing on creation
     this->enableDummyCompositionSwapchain = config.getOption<bool>("dxgi.enableDummyCompositionSwapchain", false);
     this->deferInitialFullscreen = config.getOption<bool>("dxgi.deferInitialFullscreen", false);
+    this->keepFullscreenOnFocusLoss = config.getOption<bool>("dxgi.keepFullscreenOnFocusLoss", false);
 
     // Expose Nvidia GPUs properly if NvAPI is enabled in environment
     this->hideNvidiaGpu = !isNvapiEnabled();
diff --git a/src/dxgi/dxgi_options.h b/src/dxgi/dxgi_options.h
index 69a79f7..17d49fc 100644
--- a/src/dxgi/dxgi_options.h
+++ b/src/dxgi/dxgi_options.h
@@ -61,6 +61,9 @@ namespace dxvk {
     /// Delay an initial fullscreen request until the first real present.
     bool deferInitialFullscreen;
 
+    /// Keep a non-minimized fullscreen swapchain on foreground focus loss.
+    bool keepFullscreenOnFocusLoss;
+
     /// Limit frame rate
     int32_t maxFrameRate;
 
diff --git a/src/dxgi/dxgi_swapchain.cpp b/src/dxgi/dxgi_swapchain.cpp
index ce99ae9..6b2309f 100644
--- a/src/dxgi/dxgi_swapchain.cpp
+++ b/src/dxgi/dxgi_swapchain.cpp
@@ -280,7 +280,8 @@ namespace dxvk {
           IDXGIOutput** ppTarget) {
     HRESULT hr = S_OK;
 
-    if (!m_is_d3d12 && !m_descFs.Windowed && wsi::isOccluded(m_window))
+    if (!m_is_d3d12 && !m_descFs.Windowed && wsi::isOccluded(m_window)
+     && (!m_factory->GetOptions()->keepFullscreenOnFocusLoss || wsi::isMinimized(m_window)))
       SetFullscreenState(FALSE, nullptr);
     if (pFullscreen != nullptr)
       *pFullscreen = !m_descFs.Windowed;
@@ -376,10 +377,13 @@ namespace dxvk {
       }
     }
 
-    bool occluded = !m_descFs.Windowed && wsi::isOccluded(m_window) && !wsi::isMinimized(m_window);
-
     auto options = m_factory->GetOptions();
 
+    // Wine can keep presenting fullscreen without owning keyboard focus.
+    // Do not report focus-only occlusion when preserving that presentation.
+    bool focusLost = !m_descFs.Windowed && wsi::isOccluded(m_window) && !wsi::isMinimized(m_window);
+    bool occluded = focusLost && !options->keepFullscreenOnFocusLoss;
+
     if (options->syncInterval >= 0)
       SyncInterval = options->syncInterval;
 
@@ -391,7 +395,7 @@ namespace dxvk {
     std::lock_guard<dxvk::recursive_mutex> lockWin(m_lockWindow);
     HRESULT hr = S_OK;
 
-    if (!(PresentFlags & DXGI_PRESENT_TEST) && !occluded && !wsi::isMinimized(m_window))
+    if (!(PresentFlags & DXGI_PRESENT_TEST) && !focusLost && !wsi::isMinimized(m_window))
       UpdateFullscreenResolution();
 
     if (wsi::isWindow(m_window) || !m_window) {
diff --git a/src/util/config/config.cpp b/src/util/config/config.cpp
index f45c102..e907567 100644
--- a/src/util/config/config.cpp
+++ b/src/util/config/config.cpp
@@ -293,10 +293,12 @@ namespace dxvk {
     { R"(\\MarySkelter2\.exe$)", {{
       { "d3d11.disableMsaa",                "True" },
     }} },
-    /* Final Fantasy XIV: Uses lots of HVV and    *
-     * also reads some uncached memory.           */
+    /* Final Fantasy XIV: Uses lots of HVV and reads uncached memory.
+     * Keep fullscreen on focus loss instead of restoring the saved small
+     * window, which drops Wine's fullscreen upscaling when using another monitor. */
     { R"(\\ffxiv_dx11\.exe$)", {{
       { "d3d11.cachedDynamicResources",       "vi" },
+      { "dxgi.keepFullscreenOnFocusLoss",   "True" },
     }} },
     /* Final Fantasy XV: VXAO does thousands of   *
      * draw calls with the same UAV bound         */
